/I><I> </I><I>assessment</I><I> </I><I>(Part</I><I> </I><I>IV</I><I> </I><I>below).</I><I> </I><I>(ETS/Separatio</I><I>n</I><I> </I><I>date,</I><I> </I><I>number</I><I> </I><I>of days</I><I> </I><I>leav</I><I>e</I><I> </I><I>accrued,</I><I> </I><I>PTDY</I><I> </I><I>authorized?,</I><I> </I><I>SFL-TAP</I><I> </I><I>progress,</I><I> </I><I>Career</I><I> </I><I>Skills</I><I> </I><I>Program,</I><I> </I><I>Family</I><I> </I><I>goals,</I><I> </I><I>civilia</I><I>n</I><I> </I><I>education,</I><I> </I><I>understandin</I><I>g</I><I> </I><I>benefits,</I><I> </I><I>financia</I><I>l</I><I> </I><I>planning)</I></Font></ss:Data></Cell></Row><Row ss:Index="16" ss:AutoFitHeight="0" ss:Height="409"><Cell ss:Index="1" ss:MergeAcross="13" ss:MergeDown="1" ss:StyleID="s03"><ss:Data ss:Type="String" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/TR/REC-html40"><Font html:Size="10" html:Face="Times New Roman" x:Family="Roman" html:Color="#000000">I. Introduction and Orientation&#10;</Font><Font html:Size="10" html:Face="Times New Roman" x:Family="Roman" html:Color="#000000">• Opening Remarks: Reinforce that each team member represents the U.S. Army and is expected to maintain the highest standards of conduct, discipline, and appearance at all times.&#10;</Font><Font html:Size="10" html:Face="Times New Roman" x:Family="Roman" html:Color="#000000">• Reference: TC 7-21.13, The Soldier’s Guide – emphasizes that every Soldier is responsible for maintaining Army Values, Warrior Ethos, and professional bearing both on and off duty.&#10;</Font><Font html:Size="10" html:Face="Times New Roman" x:Family="Roman" html:Color="#000000">• Focus Areas: Loyalty, Duty, Respect, Selfless Service, Honor, Integrity, and Personal Courage.&#10;</Font><Font html:Size="10" html:Face="Times New Roman" x:Family="Roman" html:Color="#000000">• Outcome: Ensure all personnel understand their role in contributing to the team’s mission and maintaining Army professionalism.&#10;</Font><Font html:Size="10" html:Face="Times New Roman" x:Family="Roman" html:Color="#000000">II. Baseline of Conduct and Responsibilities&#10;</Font><Font html:Size="10" html:Face="Times New Roman" x:Family="Roman" html:Color="#000000">• Appearance and Discipline: AR 670-1, Wear and Appearance of Army Uniforms and Insignia – all Soldiers will maintain a neat, professional, and serviceable appearance at all times.&#10;</Font><Font html:Size="10" html:Face="Times New Roman" x:Family="Roman" html:Color="#000000">• Physical Readiness: AR 600-9, The Army Body Composition Program – Soldiers must maintain physical readiness and appearance consistent with Army standards.&#10;</Font><Font html:Size="10" html:Face="Times New Roman" x:Family="Roman" html:Color="#000000">• Training Readiness: AR 350-1, Army Training and Leader Development – mandates continuous individual and collective training to sustain readiness and proficiency.&#10;</Font><Font html:Size="10" html:Face="Times New Roman" x:Family="Roman" html:Color="#000000">• Outcome: Reinforce that discipline and standards are non-negotiable components of unit readiness and effectiveness.&#10;</Font><Font html:Size="10" html:Face="Times New Roman" x:Family="Roman" html:Color="#000000">III. Adherence to Army Doctrine and Updated Policies&#10;</Font><Font html:Size="10" html:Face="Times New Roman" x:Family="Roman" html:Color="#000000">• Doctrine Familiarization: TC 7-21.13 – outlines responsibilities of Soldiers as members of a profession grounded in trust and competence.&#10;</Font><Font html:Size="10" html:Face="Times New Roman" x:Family="Roman" html:Color="#000000">• Leadership Development: TC 6-22.6, Army Team Building – promotes understanding of leadership dynamics and the principles of team development.&#10;</Font><Font html:Size="10" html:Face="Times New Roman" x:Family="Roman" html:Color="#000000">• Training Compliance: AR 350-1 – emphasizes the importance of structured, progressive, and realistic training as a foundation for operational success.&#10;</Font><Font html:Size="10" html:Face="Times New Roman" x:Family="Roman" html:Color="#000000">• Implementation: Conduct regular professional development sessions, ensure awareness of policy changes, and encourage use of the Army Publishing Directorate (APD) to access current doctrine.&#10;</Font><Font html:Size="10" html:Face="Times New Roman" x:Family="Roman" html:Color="#000000">IV. Team Cohesion and Resilience&#10;</Font><Font html:Size="10" html:Face="Times New Roman" x:Family="Roman" html:Color="#000000">• Team Dynamics: Utilize TC 6-22.6 guidance to foster communication, trust, and collaboration.&#10;</Font><Font html:Size="10" html:Face="Times New Roman" x:Family="Roman" html:Color="#000000">• Resilience Building: Encourage participation in Master Resilience Training (MRT) techniques; reinforce that resilience is critical to combat readiness and long-term well-being.&#10;</Font><Font html:Size="10" html:Face="Times New Roman" x:Family="Roman" html:Color="#000000">• Inclusive Leadership: Recognize diversity and strengths within the team; promote respect and accountability.&#10;</Font><Font html:Size="10" html:Face="Times New Roman" x:Family="Roman" html:Color="#000000">• Outcome: Develop a team identity based on mutual support, trust, and shared purpose.&#10;</Font><Font html:Size="10" html:Face="Times New Roman" x:Family="Roman" html:Color="#000000">V. Team Goals, Aspirations, and Timelines&#10;</Font><Font html:Size="10" html:Face="Times New Roman" x:Family="Roman" html:Color="#000000">• Short-Term Goals: Complete required training per AR 350-1, maintain compliance with body composition standards (AR 600-9), and ensure uniform and appearance compliance (AR 670-1).&#10;</Font><Font html:Size="10" html:Face="Times New Roman" x:Family="Roman" html:Color="#000000">• Mid-Term Goals: Enhance leadership capabilities through study and application of TC 6-22.6 and TC 7-21.13.&#10;</Font><Font html:Size="10" html:Face="Times New Roman" x:Family="Roman" html:Color="#000000">• Long-Term Goals: Build a cohesive, resilient team capable of executing missions with competence, discipline, and adaptability.&#10;</Font><Font html:Size="10" html:Face="Times New Roman" x:Family="Roman" html:Color="#000000">• Timeline:&#10;</Font><Font html:Size="10" html:Face="Times New Roman" x:Family="Roman" html:Color="#000000">◦ Initial Review: Within 30 days – verify understanding and compliance.&#10;</Font><Font html:Size="10" html:Face="Times New Roman" x:Family="Roman" html:Color="#000000">◦ Monthly Assessments: Evaluate training, readiness, and cohesion progress.&#10;</Font><Font html:Size="10" html:Face="Times New Roman" x:Family="Roman" html:Color="#000000">◦ Ad Hoc Review: Conduct comprehensive assessment tied to unit objectives and individual professional development plans when necessary.</Font></ss:Data></Cell></Row><Row ss:Index="17" ss:AutoFitHeight="0" ss:Height="37"/><Row ss:Index="18" ss:AutoFitHeight="0" ss:Height="129"><Cell ss:Index="1" ss:MergeAcross="13" ss:StyleID="s03"><ss:Data ss:Type="String" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/TR/REC-html40"><Font html:Size="8" html:Face="Arial" x:Family="Swiss" html:Color="#000000"><B>Session Closing: </B><I>(Th</I><I>e</I><I> </I><I>leader</I><I> </I><I>summarizes</I><I> </I><I>th</I><I>e</I><I> </I><I>key</I><I> </I><I>points</I><I> </I><I>of</I><I> </I><I>th</I><I>e</I><I> </I><I>sessio</I><I>n</I><I> </I><I>an</I><I>d</I><I> </I><I>checks</I><I> </I><I>if</I><I> </I><I>th</I><I>e</I><I> </I><I>subordinat</I><I>e</I><I> </I><I>understands</I><I> </I><I>th</I><I>e</I><I> </I><I>pla</I><I>n</I><I> </I><I>of</I><I> </I><I>action.</I><I> </I><I>Th</I><I>e</I><I> </I><I>subordinate </I><I>agrees</I><I> </I><I>/</I><I> </I><I>disagrees</I><I> </I><I>an</I><I>d</I><I> </I><I>provides</I><I> </I><I>remarks</I><I> </I><I>if</I><I> </I><I>appropriate.)&#10;</I></Font><Font html:Size="8" html:Face="Arial" x:Family="Swiss" html:Color="#000000">Individual counseled:    </Font><Font html:Size="8" html:Face="Arial Unicode MS" x:Family="Swiss" html:Color="#000000">✔   </Font><Font html:Size="8" html:Face="Arial" x:Family="Swiss" html:Color="#000000">I agree             disagree with the information above. Individual counseled remarks:</Font></ss:Data></Cell></Row><Row ss:Index="19" ss:AutoFitHeight="0" ss:Height="35"><Cell ss:Index="1" ss:MergeAcross="12" ss:StyleID="s06"><ss:Data ss:Type="String" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/TR/REC-html40"><Font html:Size="8" html:Face="Arial" x:Family="Swiss" html:Color="#000000">Signature of Individual Counseled:</Font></ss:Data></Cell><Cell ss:Index="14" ss:StyleID="s03"><ss:Data ss:Type="String" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/TR/REC-html40"><Font html:Size="8" html:Face="Arial" x:Family="Swiss" html:Color="#000000">DATE <I>(YYYYMMDD)</I>:</Font></ss:Data></Cell></Row><Row ss:Index="20" ss:AutoFitHeight="0" ss:Height="55"><Cell ss:Index="1" ss:MergeAcross="13" ss:StyleID="s03"><ss:Data ss:Type="String" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/TR/REC-html40"><Font html:Size="8" html:Face="Arial" x:Family="Swiss" html:Color="#000000"><B>Leader Responsibilities: </B><I>(Leader's responsibilities </I><I>i</I><I>n </I><I>implementin</I><I>g </I><I>th</I><I>e </I><I>pla</I><I>n of action.)&#10;</I></Font><Font html:Size="10" html:Face="Times New Roman" x:Family="Roman" html:Color="#000000">Leadership in accordance with TC 7-22.7, ATP 6-22.1, and ADP 7&#10;</Font><Font html:Size="10" html:Face="Times New Roman" x:Family="Roman" html:Color="#000000">Accountability to and the oversite of issues concerning with ARs 600-25, 600-32, 600-52, and 600-20</Font></ss:Data></Cell></Row><Row ss:Index="21" ss:AutoFitHeight="0" ss:Height="19"><Cell ss:Index="1" ss:MergeAcross="13" ss:StyleID="s16"><ss:Data ss:Type="String" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/TR/REC-html40"><Font html:Size="10" html:Face="Arial" x:Family="Swiss" html:Color="#000000"><B>Note:  Both the counselor and the individual counseled should retain a record of the counseling.</B></Font></ss:Data></Cell></Row><Row ss:Index="22" ss:AutoFitHeight="0" ss:Heigh